erstood what was going  on  what if they went down the frozeup creek  so as not to leave their tracks  you idiot dogs ain't that smart  interestingly houser who plays horus has  compared the characters to bert and  ernie and told comicbook.com that he  pinched bob hoskins voice from the movie  hook for the part  how can you not love this face as for  the 90s take on jasper and horus well  that  really lays the slapstick on thick  turning the purr into knock-offs of the  home alone baddies which makes sense  when you realise it was written by john  hughes who also wrote home alone  while the latest movie does follow the  original book and animation by making  anita and cruella former school friends  it breaks away from the 1996 film where  anita worked as a designer for cruella  and instead makes her a photojournalist  given how good actress kirby hal  baptiste has been in other shows she  never gets much to do  here which is a real shame looking back  there was little of interest in the  character of anita in either of the  earlier films but that was more  understandable in the animation given  its short run time and the fact the  dalmatians not  the humans were the stars when it came  to the first live action though they  somehow managed to make anita even more  bland than the animation  giving her a stereotypical 50s housewife  vibe despite the film being set in the  mid 90s  this time around roger who's played by  cave and novak  only has a small role as well he's the  baroness's lawyer and also plays piano  in a dingy little bar in a nod to the  animation where he's a songwriter and  with his wife anita  owner of the titular dalmatians as for  the 90s film where he was an american  video game designer  roger was pretty dull and actor jeff  daniels and on-screen wife jolie  richardson had almost no chemistry  in the news story roger and anita never  meet but stick around for the  mid-credits scene  as it features some easter eggs and  hints at their future together  a couple of other new characters added  to the mix are mark strong's john the  valet  an arty played by john mccree as a close  confidant to the baroness  jon knows many of her secrets and her  search plays a small but significant  role in the story  as for arty he's the lgbtq plus owner of  a vintage clothes boutique and helps  corella in her insane fashion stunts to  steal the baroness's thunder  and according to the channel mama's  geeky director craig gillespie loved  mccree's witty performance so much they  ended up adding an extra scene for him  so what do you think of disney's new  cruella do you like the changes to her  and the other characters from 101  dalmatians let me know your thoughts and  theories in the comments below  if you enjoyed this then hit that like  button and tap left for my next disney  video or tap right for something else  you're sure to like  thanks for watching and see you next  time yippee kai movie lovers

